Key Design Rules to Keep
Retrieval grounds every flag — no clause gets a risk label without at least one comparable reference clause pulled from pgvector. If similarity is too low, mark "unable to assess" instead of guessing.
Rule-layer runs independently of the LLM — deterministic red-flag keywords are a safety net even if the LLM misses something or Gemini free-tier throttles a call.
Batch everything — never call Gemini per-clause; batch 5-8 clauses/call to survive the free-tier rate limit.
Structured output only — force JSON schema on every Gemini call (use Gemini's function calling / response schema), never parse free text.
Confidence shown always — every clause card shows confidence + "not legal advice" disclaimer.

